    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy</string>
    <string name="privacy_1_t">No account, no tracking</string>
    <string name="privacy_1_b">Afterdrop has no account, no analytics, no ads and no crash reporting. Everything it keeps stays in its own storage on this phone.</string>
    <string name="privacy_2_t">Steps</string>
    <string name="privacy_2_b">Read from Health Connect on this phone to show today\'s steps and the last seven days in your widgets. Only step counts are read. They are never sent anywhere, and widgets that send data to the internet cannot use them. You can take the access back at any time in Health Connect.</string>
    <string name="privacy_3_t">What is playing</string>
    <string name="privacy_3_b">With notification access, Afterdrop asks Android which song is playing in apps that show media controls. It does not read, keep or send your notifications. Cover art is kept as a small picture in Afterdrop\'s own storage.</string>
    <string name="privacy_4_t">Calendar</string>
    <string name="privacy_4_b">Read on this phone to list your next events. Never sent anywhere.</string>
    <string name="privacy_5_t">Notes</string>
    <string name="privacy_5_b">What you write in a note widget, or share to Afterdrop, is kept on this phone only.</string>
    <string name="privacy_6_t">Internet data</string>
    <string name="privacy_6_b">Weather, air quality and exchange rates come from open-meteo.com and frankfurter.dev. Feeds and web data come only from addresses you allowed. Pictures that such data points to are downloaded from where it says.</string>
    <string name="privacy_7_t">Gemini</string>
    <string name="privacy_7_b">Only if you add your own Gemini API key: your widget descriptions, and the prompts of AI text widgets, go to Google\'s Gemini API. Private data (steps, calendar, notes, music) is never put into them.</string>
    <string name="needs_key">Add your Gemini API key in Afterdrop to see this.</string>
